        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "uint64 max_queue_size input silently truncated into uint32 global",
        "explanation": "set_max_queue_size now reads a uint64 but stores it into the static uint32_t max_queue_size with no range check. The '!value' check runs on the 64-bit value, so 4294967296 passes validation and is stored as 0. That makes every queue count as full, so enqueueing fails for every packet. Other large values wrap to arbitrary small limits. The getter (visit_type_uint32) and the registered property type ('uint32') were not changed, so the property's contract is now inconsistent too.",
        "suggestion": "Either go back to visit_type_uint32, or reject value > UINT32_MAX with an error before assigning (or widen max_queue_size, the getter and the property type together).",
        "evidence": "    visit_type_uint64(v, name, &value, &local_err);",
        "confidence": 0.85,
        "id": "1cdda53add84",
        "hunk_id": "net/colo-compare.c#3",
        "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
